# The build context is what COPY . . carries into the image. Without this file
# it was 2.2 GB, of which about 1.6 GB is neither source nor test: an RStudio
# session directory, the saved output of a previous local check, and the git
# history. Copying them makes every build slower and every layer bigger, and
# ci-check-output in particular feeds the output of this very tool back in as
# its own input.
.git
.Rproj.user
ci-check-output
dev/test-reports
*.Rcheck
.Rhistory
.RData
.Ruserdata

# NOTE: data/ is NOT excluded. In an R package it is a source directory holding
# the bundled datasets (LazyData), not a place for raw input. Excluding it made
# setup.R fail with "object 'test_master_features' not found".
